  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q01: Modularity Benefit</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>How does <strong>Modularity</strong> in OOP help in building large systems, like a car factory simulation?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Modularity reduces complexity by breaking systems into manageable, independent pieces.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0</defaultgrade>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <correctfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Your answer is correct.</p>]]></text></correctfeedback>
    <partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>]]></text></partiallycorrectfeedback>
    <incorrectfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Your answer is incorrect.</p>]]></text></incorrectfeedback>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It allows you to use more global variables.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. Modularity actually helps <strong>reduce</strong> the need for global variables.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It allows systems to be built from smaller, self-contained and independently testable components.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct! You can build and test an 'Engine' object independently of the 'Car'.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It combines all logic into a single large function.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. This describes a monolithic approach, which is the opposite of modularity.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It removes the need for data validation.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. Data validation is still critical, but it's localized inside the module (object).</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>

  <question type="multichoice">
